WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.220
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.490 --> 01:34.940
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.300 --> 01:37.850
[Episode 32]

4
01:40.120 --> 01:42.759
My friend, please accept this.

5
01:43.520 --> 01:46.360
Money has a price, but friendship is priceless.

6
01:47.200 --> 01:49.000
For seven days and seven nights,

7
01:49.229 --> 01:50.920
you worked tirelessly

8
01:51.400 --> 01:54.800
helped tens of thousands of soldiers cross the Jinsha River.

9
01:54.920 --> 01:58.120
We Red Army soldiers will never forget

10
01:55.940 --> 01:59.720
[Liu Bocheng, Chief of the General Staff of the Red Army and concurrently Commander of the Military Commission Column]

11
01:58.350 --> 02:00.400
the kindness you've shown us.

12
02:01.040 --> 02:02.100
Fellow villagers,

13
02:02.230 --> 02:05.430
until we meet again.

14
02:06.740 --> 02:07.850
Goodbye.

15
02:17.370 --> 02:19.370
[Li Kenong, Chief of Work Department of the Red Army of the National Security Bureau]

16
02:35.670 --> 02:44.630
[List of 37 boatmen: Zhang Chaoshou, Zhang Chaofu, Zhang Chaolu, Zhang Chaojing, Zhang Chaoman, Zhang Chaolian, Zhang Chaoyuan]

17
02:44.680 --> 02:56.600
[Zhang Chaofang, Zhang Chaofa, Zhang Xinggui, Zhang Zhongyin, Zhang Zouyou, Zhang Chaoxing, Yin Mengzhi, Li Rucheng, Li Youcai, Li Zhengfang]

18
02:56.650 --> 03:05.830
[Li Minglu, Chen Yueqing, Ding Ji'an, Xiao Wangyou, Zhou De'an, Zhou Qilong, Tian Xingke, Xiang Zhifu, Xiang Zhengfa]

19
03:05.890 --> 03:13.020
[Xiang Zhengjia, Luo Xingwu, Yao Guoyuan, Luo Xingquan, Zhong Yingfu, Yao Wancheng, Yan Zaihong, Kang Kun, Xiang Er the sugar maker, Pockmarked Yang]

20
03:13.400 --> 03:13.960
Cousin.

21
03:13.440 --> 03:16.600
[Kunming, Yunnan]

22
03:14.150 --> 03:15.350
Scouts in several locations have confirmed

23
03:15.350 --> 03:18.670
that the Zhu-Mao Communist forces have all crossed the river and headed north

24
03:16.600 --> 03:17.790
[Long Yun, Commander-in-Chief of the Kuomintang's 2nd Route Pursuit Army and Chairman of Yunnan Provincial Government]

25
03:19.240 --> 03:20.960
to attack Huili County.

26
03:21.280 --> 03:22.400
There are no signs of the Communist Army

27
03:22.250 --> 03:25.530
[Lu Han, Yunnan Provincial Superintendent of Militia Affairs of Kuomintang]

28
03:22.560 --> 03:24.079
left anywhere in Yunnan.

29
03:26.190 --> 03:28.310
Good, we got through this.

30
03:28.800 --> 03:31.000
Now we just have to prepare for the next.

31
03:31.829 --> 03:32.760
Let's go.

32
03:33.510 --> 03:36.370
Let's go to the airport to receive Chiang Kai-shek.

33
03:42.840 --> 03:45.790
From May 9, 1935,

34
03:45.810 --> 03:48.710
the 3rd Red Army Corps and the Commission Cadre Regiment,

35
03:48.710 --> 03:50.590
under orders from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

36
03:50.590 --> 03:53.240
launched an attack on Huili County.

37
03:53.430 --> 03:56.000
Huili was heavily fortified,

38
03:56.190 --> 03:59.560
and Liu Yuantang's Sichuan Army garrison put up fierce resistance.

39
03:59.560 --> 04:01.310
Lacking heavy weapons, the Red Army

40
04:01.310 --> 04:03.640
was unable to break through the defenses.

41
04:03.860 --> 04:06.120
The two sides were locked in a stalemate.

42
04:08.090 --> 04:12.260
[Sichuan-Xikang Border Defense Headquarters, Xichang, Sichuan]

43
04:12.310 --> 04:17.130
[Liu Yuanzhang; Liu Wenhui's nephew, Commander of KMT's Chuan-Kang Frontier Force]

44
04:13.280 --> 04:13.960
Hello?

45
04:14.150 --> 04:15.320
The Communist Army...

46
04:15.320 --> 04:17.200
They're digging tunnels outside the city wall!

47
04:17.200 --> 04:20.380
[Sichuan-Xikang Border Defense Headquarters, Xichang, Sichuan] [Liu Yuantang, Commander of the 1st Brigade of the Sichuan-Kang Border Defense Force; Nephew of Liu Wenhui, ]

48
04:17.579 --> 04:19.440
They're going to blow up the city wall!

49
04:19.440 --> 04:20.709
If I don't retreat now,

50
04:20.870 --> 04:22.680
I'll be blown sky-high.

51
04:22.830 --> 04:24.310
Yuantang, listen to me.

52
04:24.480 --> 04:25.360
You can't retreat.

53
04:25.360 --> 04:26.840
You absolutely cannot retreat!

54
04:26.840 --> 04:29.450
I've already sent the 2nd Brigade to reinforce you.

55
04:29.450 --> 04:31.390
Uncle says you must hold Huili County,

56
04:31.390 --> 04:33.000
no matter what.

57
04:33.360 --> 04:34.830
It's easy for Uncle to say!

58
04:34.950 --> 04:36.880
Let him come and defend it himself!

59
04:38.320 --> 04:39.640
Hey, bro!

60
04:39.920 --> 04:41.000
Say something!

61
04:41.570 --> 04:43.760
Yuantang, don't be foolish.

62
04:44.800 --> 04:45.310
Now Chiang is in Kunming right now,

63
04:45.310 --> 04:47.240
drawing up a plan to eliminate the Communist Army.

64
04:47.000 --> 04:50.800
[Liu Wenhui; Commander-in-Chief of the KMT's Chuan-Kang Frontier Force and Commander of the KMT's 24th Army]

65
04:47.480 --> 04:48.720
An army of over 100,000 troops

66
04:48.720 --> 04:49.950
has already reached the Jinsha River

67
04:49.950 --> 04:51.210
and will cross it soon.

68
04:51.750 --> 04:53.600
If you hold Huili County,

69
04:53.620 --> 04:55.820
you'll have done the country a great favor.

70
04:55.820 --> 04:56.730
Then I will personally

71
04:56.730 --> 04:58.290
ask Chiang to reward you.

72
04:58.950 --> 05:00.070
If you can't hold it

73
05:00.070 --> 05:01.830
and the Communist Army break through and head north...

74
05:01.830 --> 05:03.370
you won't be the only one implicated.

75
05:03.370 --> 05:05.080
Your brother and I will also be punished

76
05:05.080 --> 05:07.310
by Chiang as a warning to others, got it?

77
05:07.810 --> 05:09.220
I know, Uncle.

78
05:13.620 --> 05:14.450
Yuanzhang.

79
05:15.670 --> 05:17.600
Send another telegram to Kunming.

80
05:17.870 --> 05:19.000
This is urgent.

81
05:19.630 --> 05:20.270
Yes, sir!

82
05:23.690 --> 05:28.850
[Kunming, Yunnan]

83
05:35.560 --> 05:37.159
Sun Tzu's The Art of War says,

84
05:37.390 --> 05:38.840
"Success in warfare is gained by carefully

85
05:38.840 --> 05:41.600
accommodating ourselves to the enemy’s purpose.

86
05:41.600 --> 05:43.830
We should concentrate our forces to strike at the commander from a distance.

87
05:43.830 --> 05:46.440
This is called ability to accomplish a thing by sheer cunning."

88
05:46.440 --> 05:49.520
But no one here has shown

89
05:50.430 --> 05:51.630
that kind of ability.

90
05:52.560 --> 05:55.690
But the Communist Army has a commander who's got that ability—

91
05:55.690 --> 05:56.690
Mao Zedong.

92
05:57.040 --> 05:59.659
Since the Communist Army entered Guizhou last year,

93
05:59.659 --> 06:01.450
he's kept hundreds of thousands of our troops

94
06:01.450 --> 06:03.280
running around in circles.

95
06:04.670 --> 06:07.430
It often keeps me awake at night.

96
06:07.830 --> 06:09.360
So I'd like to ask all of you:

97
06:09.750 --> 06:12.280
if we fail to wipe out the Zhu-Mao Communist forces,

98
06:12.280 --> 06:14.540
will you be able to eat and sleep in peace?

99
06:17.070 --> 06:18.000
Generalissimo.

100
06:18.060 --> 06:19.290
Our failure to wipe out

101
06:19.290 --> 06:21.490
the Zhu-Mao Communist forces in Yunnan

102
06:21.670 --> 06:22.670
is truly a pity.

103
06:22.800 --> 06:25.440
I feel I've failed to live up to your expectations.

104
06:25.440 --> 06:27.560
I humbly ask you to hold Long Yun

105
06:27.580 --> 06:29.980
accountable to the Party for this failure.

106
06:33.870 --> 06:34.920
Also, Meng Zhiren,

107
06:34.920 --> 06:38.600
the staff officer responsible for destroying the boats after the

108
06:39.190 --> 06:42.920
river crossing has already been executed for dereliction of duty.

109
06:43.270 --> 06:44.750
Chairman Zhizhou (Long Yun).

110
06:44.750 --> 06:47.360
I'm not here to blame you this time.

111
06:47.750 --> 06:50.070
I came to work with you

112
06:50.360 --> 06:52.750
on a plan to wipe out the Zhu-Mao Communist forces

113
06:52.750 --> 06:54.950
to redeem ourselves after our failure.

114
06:55.070 --> 06:55.830
Yes, Generalissimo.

115
06:55.830 --> 06:56.720
All departments across Yunnan

116
06:56.720 --> 07:00.520
will fully cooperate with your plan to defeat the Communist forces.

117
07:00.750 --> 07:03.040
Chairman Zhizhou, do you have any suggestions?

118
07:03.040 --> 07:04.000
Please go ahead.

119
07:04.110 --> 07:05.310
Yes, Generalissimo.

120
07:05.750 --> 07:06.550
Bring it here.

121
07:13.710 --> 07:14.830
What does this mean?

122
07:14.830 --> 07:15.460
Generalissimo.

123
07:15.460 --> 07:17.360
This "More Essays from a Commonplace Hut"

124
07:17.360 --> 07:20.560
was written by Xue Fucheng, an official involved in the late Qing's Westernization Movement.

125
07:20.560 --> 07:22.720
It's a volume of "Complete Works from the Commonplace Hut."

126
07:22.720 --> 07:23.830
It tells the story of

127
07:23.830 --> 07:25.750
Shi Dakai, a general of the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom,

128
07:25.750 --> 07:28.890
whose entire army was wiped out on the banks of the Dadu River.

129
07:28.890 --> 07:32.360
I read "More Essays from a Commonplace Hut" long ago.

130
07:31.020 --> 07:35.000
[Yang Yongtai, Secretary-General of the Wuchang Field Headquarters]

131
07:33.180 --> 07:35.750
The account in this book matches what Chairman Long has just described.

132
07:35.750 --> 07:37.670
After Shi Dakai left Nanjing,

133
07:37.690 --> 07:39.070
he crossed several provinces.

134
07:39.070 --> 07:40.850
His route before his final defeat

135
07:40.850 --> 07:43.000
was quite similar to that taken by the Zhu-Mao Communist forces.

136
07:43.000 --> 07:44.860
He also entered Yunnan from Guizhou,

137
07:44.860 --> 07:46.490
then crossed the Jinsha River and headed north,

138
07:46.490 --> 07:50.220
and was ultimately annihilated on the south bank of the Dadu River.

139
07:57.930 --> 08:00.060
Chairman Zhizhou, are you suggesting

140
08:00.270 --> 08:02.620
that our KMT forces should follow the Qing army's example

141
08:02.620 --> 08:05.040
and annihilate the Communist Army forces along the Dadu River?

142
08:05.040 --> 08:06.190
Is that what you mean?

143
08:06.190 --> 08:06.820
Exactly.

144
08:07.340 --> 08:08.740
Today, the KMT forces are

145
08:08.740 --> 08:11.390
several times stronger than the Qing army was at the time.

146
08:11.390 --> 08:13.000
If we deploy our defenses properly,

147
08:13.000 --> 08:14.700
we can definitely force the Zhu-Mao Communist forces

148
08:14.700 --> 08:16.700
to suffer the same fate as Shi Dakai.

149
08:17.190 --> 08:19.040
Good. Sounds great.

150
08:20.920 --> 08:21.830
Xue Boling.

151
08:22.390 --> 08:22.920
Here.

152
08:23.190 --> 08:25.560
I'm placing Liu Wenhui's six brigades on the south bank of the Dadu River

153
08:25.560 --> 08:26.920
under your command.

154
08:27.270 --> 08:29.070
In addition to holding your existing defensive line

155
08:29.070 --> 08:30.630
of Huili, Xichang, and Dechang,

156
08:30.630 --> 08:31.700
you must also establish

157
08:31.700 --> 08:33.980
a new defensive line along the Dadu River

158
08:34.010 --> 08:35.840
to prevent the Communist Army from advancing north.

159
08:35.840 --> 08:36.890
Yes, Generalissimo!

160
08:36.890 --> 08:37.820
Zizhou (Sun Du).

161
08:38.270 --> 08:38.750
Here.

162
08:38.770 --> 08:40.730
Establish a defensive line on the west bank of the Yalong River

163
08:40.730 --> 08:42.690
[Sun Du, Commander of the 3rd Column of the 2nd Route Army of the KMT "Pursuit Army"]

164
08:40.960 --> 08:42.360
to prevent the Communist Army from advancing west.

165
08:42.360 --> 08:43.440
Yes, Generalissimo!

166
08:43.440 --> 08:44.720
The remaining units

167
08:46.240 --> 08:47.480
wil build pontoon bridges,

168
08:47.480 --> 08:48.840
cross the Jinsha River and advance north

169
08:48.840 --> 08:50.790
coordinate with the Sichuan and Yunnan forces

170
08:50.790 --> 08:53.050
to establish a new line of encirclement,

171
08:53.270 --> 08:54.720
driving the Communist Army northward.

172
08:54.720 --> 08:56.440
We must destroy the Communist Army

173
08:56.440 --> 08:58.160
in the area north of the Jinsha River,

174
08:58.160 --> 08:59.160
south of the Dadu River,

175
08:59.160 --> 09:00.750
and east of the Yalong River.

176
09:00.750 --> 09:01.860
Yes, Generalissimo!

177
09:01.860 --> 09:07.060
[Tiechang Village, Suburbs of Huili, Sichuan]

178
09:05.000 --> 09:07.400
Comrade Zedong, what book are you reading?

179
09:08.530 --> 09:10.190
"More Essays from a Commonplace Hut."

180
09:10.190 --> 09:12.320
Is that the one written by Xue Fucheng?

181
09:12.360 --> 09:14.390
How is it? Any thoughts?

182
09:15.520 --> 09:16.780
In Xue Fucheng's eyes,

183
09:17.190 --> 09:19.830
Shi Dakai was just a bandit.

184
09:20.120 --> 09:22.650
What could a bandit like him ever accomplish?

185
09:23.120 --> 09:24.790
The author's biased language and one-sided account

186
09:24.790 --> 09:26.520
can't necessarily be trusted.

187
09:26.690 --> 09:28.520
But Shi Dakai

188
09:28.550 --> 09:30.820
did lack strategic foresight.

189
09:34.120 --> 09:36.570
Commander-in-Chief, what's the situation at the front?

190
09:36.570 --> 09:38.820
The Sichuan Army is relying on its fortifications

191
09:38.820 --> 09:40.680
to hold Huili County at all costs.

192
09:42.400 --> 09:45.260
We still can't break through their defensive line.

193
09:46.360 --> 09:47.340
Xue Yue's pursuing forces

194
09:47.340 --> 09:48.840
have already begun building pontoon bridges

195
09:48.840 --> 09:50.150
on the south bank of the Jinsha River.

196
09:50.150 --> 09:51.840
We don't have much time left.

197
09:52.150 --> 09:53.520
Comrade Peng Dehuai and Comrade Yang Shangkun

198
09:53.520 --> 09:54.450
suggested that we

199
09:54.450 --> 09:56.380
abandon the attack on Huili County

200
09:56.470 --> 09:57.830
to avoid being pinned down by the enemy.

201
09:57.830 --> 09:59.520
We should move north quickly

202
09:59.630 --> 10:01.460
and cross the Dadu River as soon as possible.

203
10:01.460 --> 10:02.940
Peng and Yang made a good point.

204
10:02.940 --> 10:05.150
We don't necessarily have to capture

205
10:05.280 --> 10:06.920
this Huili County.

206
10:07.990 --> 10:10.520
If we can win, we fight. If we can't, we move on.

207
10:10.920 --> 10:13.580
The problem is that if we advance farther north,

208
10:13.670 --> 10:15.730
we'll face endless mountain ranges.

209
10:15.840 --> 10:18.440
I'm concerned that the troops in the field army

210
10:18.630 --> 10:19.930
will start complaining.

211
10:19.930 --> 10:21.930
We can't stop moving forward

212
10:22.360 --> 10:23.670
just because people are complaining.

213
10:23.670 --> 10:25.510
Otherwise, we'll become another Shi Dakai.

214
10:25.510 --> 10:28.170
It's not simply a matter of people complaining.

215
10:28.550 --> 10:30.210
This is a letter from Lin Biao.

216
10:30.220 --> 10:31.750
Comrade Lin Biao thinks that

217
10:31.750 --> 10:33.020
making the troops march such a long distance

218
10:33.020 --> 10:33.840
along the longer outer route,

219
10:33.840 --> 10:35.510
rather than taking the shorter route, is a mistake.

220
10:35.510 --> 10:36.100
In addition,

221
10:36.100 --> 10:38.910
he also proposed changes to the Military Commission's command structure.

222
10:38.910 --> 10:40.470
He suggested that Comrade Zedong,

223
10:40.470 --> 10:42.330
Comrade Enlai and Comrade Zhu De,

224
10:42.440 --> 10:44.150
accompany the army and oversee the overall strategy,

225
10:44.150 --> 10:47.750
while Comrade Peng Dehuai would serve as the frontline commander,

226
10:47.750 --> 10:49.640
lead the Red Army north as quickly as possible

227
10:49.640 --> 10:51.770
to join forces with the 4th Front Army.

228
11:06.770 --> 11:08.630
This is Lin Biao's second letter.

229
11:08.830 --> 11:11.020
His first letter came after the Gutian Conference.

230
11:11.020 --> 11:13.620
He wrote to me on New Year's Day in 1930,

231
11:14.480 --> 11:17.810
expressing a very pessimistic assessment of the situation

232
11:18.050 --> 11:20.690
and little confidence in the future.

233
11:20.980 --> 11:22.240
I wrote back to tell him

234
11:22.440 --> 11:24.640
a single spark can start a prairie fire.

235
11:24.910 --> 11:27.320
This situation is much the same as before.

236
11:28.200 --> 11:29.930
This isn't just about Lin Biao.

237
11:30.150 --> 11:32.440
It reflects the mood among lower-ranking officers and soldiers.

238
11:32.440 --> 11:33.740
If we don't address this as soon as possible,

239
11:33.740 --> 11:36.000
it will undermine unity within the army.

240
11:36.370 --> 11:39.200
It could determine the outcome of the entire operation.

241
11:39.200 --> 11:40.530
That's certainly true.

242
11:40.870 --> 11:42.200
Besides the 1st Corps,

243
11:42.600 --> 11:45.270
we've heard the same concerns from other units.

244
11:45.790 --> 11:46.670
I suggest

245
11:47.550 --> 11:49.810
we hold an enlarged Politburo meeting immediately

246
11:49.810 --> 11:51.410
to discuss Lin Biao's letter

247
11:52.120 --> 11:53.360
openly and honestly.

248
11:53.720 --> 11:56.030
We need to talk about the effectiveness of

249
11:56.030 --> 11:58.340
the Military Commission's command since the Zunyi Conference.

250
11:58.340 --> 12:00.540
Then let's not make this letter public.

251
12:01.030 --> 12:02.620
It must be made public.

252
12:02.900 --> 12:03.780
Not only that,

253
12:03.970 --> 12:06.410
we should mimeograph a copy for every soldier and officer to read.

254
12:06.410 --> 12:09.870
We should let everyone read it carefully before we discuss it.

255
12:35.600 --> 12:38.000
On May 12, 1935,

256
12:38.710 --> 12:39.900
the Central Politburo

257
12:39.900 --> 12:41.830
held an enlarged meeting at an ironworks

258
12:41.830 --> 12:43.230
in the suburbs of Huili.

259
12:44.360 --> 12:46.260
Zhang Wentian hosted the meeting,

260
12:46.260 --> 12:47.730
and, in his report,

261
12:47.760 --> 12:50.360
he endorsed the Central Red Army's command

262
12:50.380 --> 12:53.400
after the establishment of the Troika military group.

263
12:53.400 --> 12:54.930
The meeting fully endorsed

264
12:55.000 --> 12:57.370
the Central Revolutionary Military Commission's strategic policy

265
12:57.370 --> 12:59.430
of highly mobile warfare that had been adopted

266
12:59.430 --> 13:01.030
since the Zunyi Conference.

267
13:01.390 --> 13:03.650
The meeting also strongly criticized the mistaken views

268
13:03.650 --> 13:05.580
expressed in Lin Biao's letter.

269
13:12.050 --> 13:14.720
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

270
13:15.320 --> 13:16.030
Comrades.

271
13:18.870 --> 13:20.070
The Zunyi Conference

272
13:20.430 --> 13:23.040
has just reorganized our military leadership.

273
13:22.920 --> 13:26.780
[Peng Dehuai Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

274
13:23.390 --> 13:24.390
At this moment,

275
13:24.800 --> 13:28.240
proposing another change to the command structure at the front

276
13:28.240 --> 13:29.390
is inappropriate.

277
13:29.850 --> 13:31.370
As for Comrade Lin Biao's proposal

278
13:31.370 --> 13:34.170
that I should serve as the frontline commander...

279
13:34.440 --> 13:36.500
that would be even less appropriate.

280
13:38.360 --> 13:40.240
Comrade Lin Biao, if you have something to say,

281
13:39.150 --> 13:42.370
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), General Leader of CPC Central Committee]

282
13:40.600 --> 13:43.000
you should raise it openly at this meeting.

283
13:53.670 --> 13:56.550
I meant nothing else by writing to the Central Committee.

284
13:56.550 --> 13:59.200
It's mainly because we've been constantly on the march

285
13:59.200 --> 14:00.590
and I've been feeling deeply frustrated.

286
14:00.590 --> 14:02.120
You're just a young fellow.

287
14:02.160 --> 14:03.120
What do you know?

288
14:03.680 --> 14:04.720
Do you think you are something special

289
14:04.720 --> 14:06.070
just because you won a few battles?

290
14:06.070 --> 14:08.130
You think you are the best in the world

291
14:08.540 --> 14:10.800
and you're getting too big for your boots?

292
14:10.800 --> 14:13.720
Without the collective efforts of our Red Army's commanders and soldiers,

293
14:13.720 --> 14:15.270
even if you had superhuman abilities,

294
14:15.270 --> 14:16.860
could command the wind and rain or conjure up an army out of thin air,

295
14:16.860 --> 14:18.210
you still couldn't win the battle by yourself!

296
14:18.210 --> 14:19.870
You couldn't conquer the world alone!

297
14:19.870 --> 14:21.070
But now many comrades

298
14:21.200 --> 14:22.550
have complaints about the constant marching.

299
14:22.550 --> 14:24.510
We keep taking the long outer route instead of the shorter inner one,

300
14:24.510 --> 14:25.870
and the troops are exhausted.

301
14:25.870 --> 14:26.790
That is a real, practical concern.

302
14:26.790 --> 14:29.440
Who would choose the longer route if the shorter one were available?

303
14:29.440 --> 14:30.800
The real question is whether,

304
14:30.800 --> 14:33.110
with large enemy forces pursuing and intercepting us at every turn,

305
14:33.110 --> 14:35.370
would they let us take the shorter route?

306
14:35.440 --> 14:37.560
It's understandable that soldiers think this way.

307
14:37.560 --> 14:40.290
But as a senior commander, you should know better

308
14:40.860 --> 14:42.120
than to think this way.

309
14:49.170 --> 14:49.880
I know

310
14:50.170 --> 14:52.390
that Lin Biao is not the only one who feels this way.

311
14:52.390 --> 14:53.660
Since the Second Crossing of the Chishui River,

312
14:53.660 --> 14:55.250
many comrades have reported to the Central Committee

313
14:55.250 --> 14:57.050
that all this constant marching

314
14:57.750 --> 14:59.210
would wear the troops out.

315
14:59.360 --> 15:00.960
Enlai, I think

316
15:01.790 --> 15:04.240
we need to clarify a few things today.

317
15:07.060 --> 15:07.990
Comrades,

318
15:08.840 --> 15:11.910
there are some circumstances you may not be aware of.

319
15:12.090 --> 15:13.360
Over the past few months,

320
15:13.360 --> 15:16.070
our Military Commission's Second Bureau has deciphered a lot of

321
15:16.070 --> 15:19.470
intelligence on enemy's troop movements and dispositions.

322
15:19.510 --> 15:20.690
Only a handful of leaders

323
15:20.690 --> 15:23.320
of the Military Commission knew about this intelligence.

324
15:23.320 --> 15:24.360
The situation was urgent.

325
15:24.360 --> 15:26.570
There simply wasn't time to inform everyone,

326
15:26.570 --> 15:28.500
so we had to issue the orders first.

327
15:28.560 --> 15:30.290
And what happened afterward proved

328
15:30.290 --> 15:33.220
that taking the longer route was the right decision.

329
15:34.720 --> 15:35.550
Comrades,

330
15:35.570 --> 15:37.960
we are not like Xiang Yu, the self-willed King of Chu.

331
15:37.960 --> 15:40.550
Nor will we be indecisive like Yuan Shao (Yuan Benchu).

332
15:40.550 --> 15:41.790
Since Zunyi Conference,

333
15:41.790 --> 15:43.090
we haven't won every battle.

334
15:43.090 --> 15:45.240
We suffered a serious defeat at Tucheng.

335
15:45.240 --> 15:46.790
We were also defeated at Lubanchang.

336
15:46.790 --> 15:48.020
Then why are we still sticking to

337
15:48.020 --> 15:49.680
our original strategic plan?

338
15:50.390 --> 15:52.550
Why are we ignoring the fatigue of the troops?

339
15:52.550 --> 15:54.140
Why cross the Chishui River four times?

340
15:54.140 --> 15:55.620
Why advance to Guiyang

341
15:55.920 --> 15:57.520
make a feint toward Kunming?

342
15:57.750 --> 15:59.820
Today, I'm going to explain it

343
16:00.100 --> 16:01.320
once and for all.

344
16:02.320 --> 16:04.910
Explain it once and for all.

345
16:05.630 --> 16:07.320
The Four Crossings of the Chishui River

346
16:07.320 --> 16:08.870
was a brilliant strategic maneuver

347
16:08.870 --> 16:12.040
that saved the Red Army from the brink of disaster.

348
16:12.740 --> 16:15.610
advancing toward Guiyang and feinting toward Kunming

349
16:15.610 --> 16:16.750
was a brilliant series of moves

350
16:16.750 --> 16:19.150
that kept a powerful enemy off balance.

351
16:20.340 --> 16:23.150
"Warm the steep cliffs lapped by the water of Jinsha."

352
16:23.150 --> 16:24.550
That marked a major breakthrough

353
16:24.550 --> 16:26.390
for tens of thousands of Red Army soldiers

354
16:26.390 --> 16:28.450
to regain the strategic initiative.

355
16:30.880 --> 16:31.790
Comrades,

356
16:32.110 --> 16:33.630
this is what war is like.

357
16:34.000 --> 16:37.120
The enemy situation doesn't change just because we want it to.

358
16:37.120 --> 16:38.230
We may intend to do one thing,

359
16:38.230 --> 16:39.720
but things don't always go as planned.

360
16:39.720 --> 16:40.480
By the time

361
16:40.730 --> 16:42.440
we got back from a detour,

362
16:42.890 --> 16:44.250
it was already done.

363
16:44.790 --> 16:45.600
So,

364
16:45.620 --> 16:48.190
we must sometimes defend before attacking.

365
16:48.720 --> 16:51.320
To advance, we may have to retreat for a while.

366
16:51.490 --> 16:52.570
To strike head-on,

367
16:52.590 --> 16:54.640
we may need to maneuver around the enemy.

368
16:54.640 --> 16:55.880
To reach our goal,

369
16:56.160 --> 16:57.960
we have to take the longer route.

370
16:58.290 --> 16:59.290
Once I make a move,

371
16:59.320 --> 17:00.440
the enemy has to respond.

372
17:00.440 --> 17:02.260
Just when they think they've surrounded us,

373
17:02.260 --> 17:04.319
we make a giant stride and move again.

374
17:04.710 --> 17:06.710
War cannot be waged by simply following a textbook.

375
17:06.710 --> 17:08.060
Chiang Kai-shek may know the military texts

376
17:08.060 --> 17:10.099
you read even better than you do.

377
17:09.970 --> 17:11.560
[Li De, Military Adviser of the Communist International]

378
17:10.680 --> 17:11.880
Copying them blindly

379
17:12.030 --> 17:13.839
will only leave you on the defensive.

380
17:13.839 --> 17:14.650
As the saying goes,

381
17:14.650 --> 17:17.930
"The clever combatant imposes his will on the enemy, but does not allow the enemy's will to be imposed on him."

382
17:17.930 --> 17:19.490
That sums it up perfectly!

383
17:19.900 --> 17:21.730
In the Red Army's own words,

384
17:22.000 --> 17:23.460
it comes down to two words:

385
17:23.660 --> 17:25.190
flexibility and mobility.

386
17:25.440 --> 17:26.599
Leaders.

387
17:29.200 --> 17:29.800
Chairman.

388
17:30.030 --> 17:31.190
It's about to get dark.

389
17:31.190 --> 17:34.620
[Liu Ying, Secretary-General of the Central Column]

390
17:31.280 --> 17:32.960
The enemy aircraft are unlikely to appear.

391
17:32.960 --> 17:35.220
We can continue the meeting at Ping'an Temple.

392
17:35.220 --> 17:36.950
Let me finish what I have to say.

393
17:37.920 --> 17:38.830
Comrades,

394
17:39.070 --> 17:40.310
we must

395
17:40.680 --> 17:43.240
reach a common understanding of

396
17:43.480 --> 17:44.970
military strategy and operational command

397
17:44.970 --> 17:46.550
as established since the Zunyi Conference.

398
17:46.550 --> 17:48.350
We must firmly carry out

399
17:48.450 --> 17:50.850
our strategic plan to establish a revolutionary base

400
17:50.850 --> 17:52.910
in western or northwestern Sichuan.

401
17:53.100 --> 17:54.760
If anyone has anything to add,

402
17:55.240 --> 17:56.970
let's discuss it openly today.

403
17:57.610 --> 17:58.140
Let's go.

404
17:58.570 --> 18:01.170
Let's continue the meeting at Ping'an Temple.

405
18:02.440 --> 18:04.040
In the subsequent meetings,

406
18:04.400 --> 18:06.750
the Politburo focused on summarizing

407
18:06.750 --> 18:08.920
the Central Red Army's extensive experience

408
18:08.920 --> 18:10.550
in mobile warfare,

409
18:10.960 --> 18:13.300
and unified the army's strategic thinking,

410
18:13.300 --> 18:15.610
and forged a common understanding of military strategy

411
18:15.610 --> 18:18.610
and operational command since the Zunyi Conference.

412
18:18.640 --> 18:20.840
This strengthen unity within the army.

413
18:21.090 --> 18:22.620
The meeting also discussed

414
18:22.790 --> 18:25.240
the plan for future operations after crossing the Jinsha River,

415
18:25.240 --> 18:27.770
decided to abandon the attack on Huili County

416
18:27.810 --> 18:29.150
and continue heading north

417
18:29.150 --> 18:31.280
to join forces with the 4th Front Army.

418
18:31.440 --> 18:33.240
The army captured Dechang,

419
18:33.370 --> 18:36.480
bypassed Xichang, which was heavily guarded by the Sichuan Army,

420
18:36.480 --> 18:39.240
captured Lizhou on May 20,

421
18:39.270 --> 18:42.740
and advanced to the Lugu area south of Mianning County.

422
18:49.510 --> 18:51.370
Only when you step out of the water

423
18:51.520 --> 18:53.370
do you see the mud on your legs.

424
18:54.260 --> 18:55.830
For over 100 days

425
18:56.110 --> 18:59.000
the fate of the CPC Central Committee and the Central Red Army

426
18:59.000 --> 19:01.880
seemed to mirror the waters they crossed: the Chishui River they crossed four times;

427
19:01.880 --> 19:05.610
the Wujiang River they crossed southward and the Jinsha River they crossed northward.

428
19:05.610 --> 19:09.450
All flowing with countless unexpected twists and endless possibilities.

429
19:09.450 --> 19:10.930
The command center's role

430
19:11.200 --> 19:13.640
was to ensure that they retained control

431
19:13.660 --> 19:16.070
over their own destiny in their own hands.

432
19:16.330 --> 19:18.340
Mao Zedong's wisdom and sense of responsibility,

433
19:18.340 --> 19:20.010
his leadership and authority,

434
19:20.010 --> 19:23.250
were tested and affirmed in times of crisis.

435
19:23.670 --> 19:26.580
After enduring so much hardship, CPC Central Committee and the Red Army

436
19:26.580 --> 19:28.120
came to fully trust Mao Zedong

437
19:28.120 --> 19:31.030
at the Huili Conference,

438
19:31.120 --> 19:33.330
115 days after the Zunyi Conference.

439
19:33.590 --> 19:35.120
The expedition of the Red Army

440
19:35.120 --> 19:38.750
thus entered a new chapter in its legendary march.

441
19:38.890 --> 19:45.180
[The Second Bureau of the Central Military Commission in Lugu, Sichuan]

442
19:39.520 --> 19:41.890
The telegram contains 247 words in total.

443
19:43.000 --> 19:45.410
The code 2074 appears nine times

444
19:46.030 --> 19:48.680
and code 6135 appears six times.

445
19:49.070 --> 19:51.400
Together, these two number groups

446
19:51.400 --> 19:53.240
appeared five times in total.

447
19:53.690 --> 19:56.060
What word would appear

448
19:56.220 --> 19:58.220
repeatedly in a single telegram?

449
19:58.000 --> 19:59.960
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff of the 2nd Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

450
19:58.590 --> 20:00.250
Could it be a unit designation

451
20:00.590 --> 20:03.100
or the name of a brigade or regiment commander?

452
20:03.100 --> 20:04.100
That makes sense.

453
20:05.270 --> 20:07.330
Chen, go to the Enemy Work Department

454
20:07.340 --> 20:09.080
and ask which unit designations the prisoners had given us.

455
20:09.080 --> 20:09.610
Yes, sir.

456
20:11.160 --> 20:11.880
Wei.

457
20:12.880 --> 20:14.220
Wei, you're finally back.

458
20:14.220 --> 20:15.330
Wei.

459
20:15.540 --> 20:17.530
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

460
20:15.600 --> 20:16.350
You must be exhausted.

461
20:16.350 --> 20:17.070
I'm fine.

462
20:17.270 --> 20:18.090
Here, give it to me.

463
20:18.090 --> 20:20.290
When did you get back from the 9th Corps?

464
20:20.310 --> 20:21.920
The corps reached Lizhou just last night.

465
20:21.920 --> 20:23.400
The Corps Commander came to report to the Military Commission,

466
20:23.400 --> 20:24.550
so I came along.

467
20:26.030 --> 20:27.000
There you are, lad!

468
20:27.000 --> 20:27.790
Director.

469
20:28.790 --> 20:30.120
Let me have a look at you.

470
20:31.490 --> 20:32.290
Not bad.

471
20:32.320 --> 20:33.520
It's been two months,

472
20:33.880 --> 20:35.040
and you've gotten darker

473
20:35.040 --> 20:35.810
and thinner.

474
20:36.170 --> 20:38.430
You're more than just an instructor now.

475
20:38.570 --> 20:41.170
Your codebreaking skills have also improved.

476
20:41.400 --> 20:42.070
Director,

477
20:42.510 --> 20:44.340
you have no objection to Wei joining the Decryption Section

478
20:43.290 --> 20:45.110
[Cao Xiangren, Section Chief of the Second Bureau of Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

479
20:44.400 --> 20:45.470
this time, do you?

480
20:46.570 --> 20:47.770
Comrade Wei Yueqiao,

481
20:48.270 --> 20:49.310
welcome back to the team.

482
20:49.310 --> 20:50.310
Starting today,

483
20:50.450 --> 20:52.830
you are officially joining the Decryption Section.

484
20:52.830 --> 20:54.720
I hope you will continue to work hard

485
20:54.720 --> 20:57.350
and soon become an expert codebreaker.

486
20:57.830 --> 20:58.550
Yes, sir!

487
20:58.800 --> 20:59.460
Have a seat.

488
20:59.480 --> 21:01.660
You must be exhausted. Sit down and rest a while.

489
21:01.660 --> 21:02.380
By the way,

490
21:02.410 --> 21:03.020
comrades,

491
21:03.100 --> 21:04.480
look what I've brought!

492
21:04.920 --> 21:06.650
Gifts! You still thought of us!

493
21:08.740 --> 21:11.150
This is Xuanwei ham.

494
21:11.230 --> 21:12.280
I saved this for all of you.

495
21:12.280 --> 21:13.120
And this,

496
21:13.680 --> 21:14.720
salt from Piao'erjing.

497
21:14.720 --> 21:15.340
Director.

498
21:16.880 --> 21:18.340
I also brought some Pu'er tea we'd seized.

499
21:18.340 --> 21:19.720
You can drink it for those late nights at work.

500
21:19.720 --> 21:20.640
-This is good. -Yeah.

501
21:20.640 --> 21:21.400
Good.

502
21:22.200 --> 21:23.610
Careful, it's hot.

503
21:24.420 --> 21:25.220
What is this?

504
21:26.920 --> 21:27.720
This?

505
21:27.920 --> 21:28.950
It's butter.

506
21:29.350 --> 21:31.550
I ate a tin of Qian's lard last time,

507
21:31.570 --> 21:33.770
so I thought I'd give him this in return.

508
21:33.790 --> 21:34.590
Qian.

509
21:35.270 --> 21:36.050
Qian.

510
21:39.260 --> 21:40.370
Where is Qian?

511
21:51.980 --> 21:53.970
Director, where is Qian?

512
21:56.730 --> 21:58.170
Comrade Qian Zhuangfei,

513
21:58.720 --> 22:00.720
went missing while we were crossing

514
22:01.880 --> 22:03.110
the Wujiang River on our way south.

515
22:03.110 --> 22:04.110
It's possible...

516
22:07.050 --> 22:08.780
that he may have given his life.

517
22:34.000 --> 22:35.130
Vice Chairman Zhou.

518
22:35.680 --> 22:36.850
Vice Chairman Zhou.

519
22:42.060 --> 22:43.340
Vice Chairman Zhou.

520
22:45.030 --> 22:45.830
Don't cry.

521
22:51.790 --> 22:54.250
After Comrade Qian Zhuangfei went missing,

522
22:56.440 --> 23:00.030
the Military Commission sent several search teams

523
23:00.050 --> 23:01.940
along the river to search for him.

524
23:02.240 --> 23:03.900
We all feel the same way you do,

525
23:04.310 --> 23:06.920
hoping he's only missing for the time being.

526
23:09.680 --> 23:12.720
Comrade Qian Zhuangfei made

527
23:13.110 --> 23:14.880
great contributions to the revolution.

528
23:14.880 --> 23:16.070
If it weren't for him,

529
23:16.070 --> 23:18.350
many comrades, including myself,

530
23:18.550 --> 23:20.150
might not have had the chance

531
23:20.210 --> 23:22.010
to continue serving the Party.

532
23:23.100 --> 23:24.170
Rest assured.

533
23:25.400 --> 23:27.020
As long as there's even the slightest hope,

534
23:27.020 --> 23:28.860
we will keep searching for him.

535
23:33.100 --> 23:34.700
This is the book Qian gave me.

536
23:36.490 --> 23:38.380
I've read it three times already.

537
23:40.890 --> 23:43.290
I've always wanted to come back and tell him

538
23:44.350 --> 23:45.840
that I have changed.

539
23:58.630 --> 24:00.760
Our lives

540
24:01.380 --> 24:04.060
may be short and insignificant,

541
24:04.310 --> 24:05.270
but

542
24:05.910 --> 24:07.520
all great things

543
24:07.940 --> 24:11.180
are accomplished by human hands.

544
24:12.860 --> 24:14.500
To realize

545
24:14.880 --> 24:16.680
that one has

546
24:18.070 --> 24:20.270
such a noble task in life—

547
24:21.000 --> 24:24.440
that is the highest happiness

548
24:25.000 --> 24:27.310
a person can know.

549
24:46.860 --> 24:52.610
[Military Commission's Temporary Encampment, Lugu, Sichuan]

550
24:47.110 --> 24:48.680
The Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

551
24:48.680 --> 24:50.880
fights for the liberation of oppressed ethnic minorities.

552
24:50.880 --> 24:52.680
All Yi and Han people

553
24:53.080 --> 24:54.750
are brothers and sisters.

554
24:55.070 --> 24:56.550
The Sichuan warlords are cruel;

555
24:56.550 --> 24:58.400
they oppress the Yi people mercilessly.

556
24:58.400 --> 25:00.510
They burden the people with exorbitant taxes and levies

557
25:00.510 --> 25:02.110
and kill people at will.

558
25:02.350 --> 25:03.880
The Red Army's long march

559
25:04.100 --> 25:06.410
is now unstoppable.

560
25:06.440 --> 25:08.760
We've marched over 5,000 kilometers?

561
25:08.950 --> 25:11.640
A strategic shift from the Central Soviet Area

562
25:12.160 --> 25:14.730
has turned into a long march across the country.

563
25:14.730 --> 25:17.000
We've probably marched more than 5,000 kilometers.

564
25:17.000 --> 25:18.160
Who knows

565
25:18.160 --> 25:20.220
how much farther we'll have to march?

566
25:20.250 --> 25:23.110
We've tried to establish base in several places, but we failed.

567
25:23.110 --> 25:26.000
I'm afraid we'll have to keep moving.

568
25:27.400 --> 25:28.880
On this long march

569
25:29.350 --> 25:30.790
of over 5,000 kilometers,

570
25:30.790 --> 25:32.340
we've survived one danger after another,

571
25:32.340 --> 25:34.200
fighting to the death to survive.

572
25:34.780 --> 25:36.650
We must keep marching

573
25:37.400 --> 25:39.930
and rise anew from the ashes like the phoenix.

574
25:41.930 --> 25:43.250
I think Comrade Lu Dingyi's

575
25:43.250 --> 25:44.740
proclamation is very well written.

576
25:44.740 --> 25:45.920
Each line has multiople words,

577
25:45.920 --> 25:47.810
with a consistent rhyme and a natural rhythm.

578
25:47.810 --> 25:49.700
It's a proclamation written like a poem.

579
25:49.700 --> 25:50.310
Indeed.

580
25:50.450 --> 25:52.880
It effectively expresses our Party's ethnic policy,

581
25:52.880 --> 25:54.680
which is crucial to carrying out

582
25:54.710 --> 25:56.040
our strategic mission.

583
25:56.050 --> 25:57.680
I suggest we publish the proclamation

584
25:57.680 --> 25:59.550
under the Commander-in-Chief's name.

585
25:59.550 --> 26:00.310
Agreed.

586
26:00.890 --> 26:02.390
Now that we've reached agreement in principle,

587
26:02.390 --> 26:04.410
we need to deal with the practical issues.

588
26:04.410 --> 26:05.050
Bocheng,

589
26:06.840 --> 26:09.190
tell us about our current situation.

590
26:09.450 --> 26:10.150
Okay.

591
26:11.490 --> 26:13.250
Based on the intelligence from

592
26:13.680 --> 26:15.720
the Military Commission's Second Bureau and the

593
26:15.720 --> 26:17.050
underground Party organization in Mianning,

594
26:17.050 --> 26:19.380
the Sichuan Army's forces are currently

595
26:20.000 --> 26:22.960
assembled on the north bank of the Dadu River,

596
26:23.510 --> 26:25.160
and the south bank is only lightly defended.

597
26:25.160 --> 26:27.270
From Lugu to the Dadu River,

598
26:27.360 --> 26:28.710
there are two routes in total.

599
26:28.710 --> 26:31.710
One is the main road to Chengdu and Ya'an,

600
26:31.810 --> 26:34.370
which is heavily guarded by KMT troops.

601
26:34.790 --> 26:35.720
The other road

602
26:35.860 --> 26:37.600
runs from Lugu through Mianning

603
26:37.600 --> 26:40.150
to Anshunchang beside the Dadu River.

604
26:40.420 --> 26:41.820
But it's a mountain road,

605
26:42.160 --> 26:43.120
so the terrain is difficult,

606
26:43.120 --> 26:45.470
and we have to pass through the settlement where the Yi people live.

607
26:45.470 --> 26:47.640
However, the KMT army's defense

608
26:47.830 --> 26:48.880
is relatively weak there.

609
26:48.880 --> 26:50.610
Which route do you have in mind?

610
26:50.670 --> 26:51.400
I suggest

611
26:51.960 --> 26:54.220
we send a small force along the main road,

612
26:54.410 --> 26:56.150
to make the enemy think we're going to cross the river there

613
26:56.150 --> 26:58.410
and launch a surprise attack on Chengdu.

614
26:58.720 --> 27:00.130
Meanwhile, the main Red Army force

615
27:00.130 --> 27:02.390
should immediately change course to catch the enemy off guard,

616
27:02.390 --> 27:03.740
head northwest through Mianning,

617
27:03.740 --> 27:04.810
pass through Yi-inhabited area,

618
27:04.810 --> 27:06.130
head straight for Anshunchang

619
27:06.130 --> 27:07.860
and cross the river from there.

620
27:09.110 --> 27:09.720
Bocheng,

621
27:10.180 --> 27:11.720
you and the Commander-in-Chief

622
27:11.720 --> 27:13.270
are thinking alike.

623
27:14.680 --> 27:15.480
What?

624
27:16.110 --> 27:18.750
You all had the same plan, too?

625
27:18.920 --> 27:19.680
Bocheng.

626
27:19.960 --> 27:20.740
I've discussed this with Mao,

627
27:20.740 --> 27:22.500
Enlai and Jiaxiang.

628
27:22.770 --> 27:24.720
We decided to form an advance unit

629
27:24.920 --> 27:26.370
to move ahead of the main force

630
27:26.370 --> 27:27.610
and clear the way.

631
27:28.130 --> 27:29.810
And you will be the Commander

632
27:30.390 --> 27:31.150
of this unit.

633
27:31.400 --> 27:32.030
Okay.

634
27:32.550 --> 27:34.640
The advance unit will consist of the 1st Red Regiment

635
27:34.640 --> 27:36.000
and the Headquarters Work Group,

636
27:36.000 --> 27:37.260
led by Comrade Xiao Hua

637
27:37.360 --> 27:39.120
and Comrade Feng Wenbin.

638
27:39.550 --> 27:41.880
Given the actual situation in the Yi area,

639
27:42.090 --> 27:45.030
we'll also reinforce it with the reconnaissance company

640
27:45.030 --> 27:46.970
and the engineer-sapper company of the 1st Army Corps.

641
27:46.970 --> 27:47.700
Understood.

642
27:47.990 --> 27:49.580
Comrade Luo Ruiqing was originally appointed

643
27:49.580 --> 27:51.720
as the Political Commissar of the advance unit.

644
27:51.720 --> 27:53.160
But he's ill now.

645
27:53.360 --> 27:55.850
So we'll replace him with another Sichuan native:

646
27:55.850 --> 27:56.840
Comrade Nie Rongzhen.

647
27:56.840 --> 27:57.840
What do you think?

648
27:58.030 --> 28:00.620
Comrade Nie Rongzhen is well suited to the role.

649
28:00.620 --> 28:01.210
Good.

650
28:02.200 --> 28:02.730
Bocheng.

651
28:04.010 --> 28:06.450
Do you know the legend of the Yi region?

652
28:07.200 --> 28:07.920
I do.

653
28:08.070 --> 28:10.310
Legend has it that, during the Three Kingdoms period, that was

654
28:10.310 --> 28:12.510
the place where Zhuge Liang captured and released Meng Huo seven times.

655
28:12.510 --> 28:14.310
When Zhuge Liang marched south,

656
28:14.340 --> 28:16.400
he didn't rely on military force alone,

657
28:16.400 --> 28:18.460
instead, he captured and released Meng Huo seven times

658
28:18.460 --> 28:21.190
to win the hearts of the local ethnic minorities.

659
28:22.000 --> 28:22.790
Chairman,

660
28:22.840 --> 28:24.240
do you also want me

661
28:24.790 --> 28:26.250
to learn from Zhuge Liang?

662
28:26.320 --> 28:27.780
You should learn from him.

663
28:28.550 --> 28:30.350
But you can't copy everything he did.

664
28:30.350 --> 28:31.110
So...

665
28:31.360 --> 28:33.600
we will give you a bag of tricks.

666
28:34.160 --> 28:35.350
A bag of tricks?

667
28:36.550 --> 28:37.350
Great.

668
28:45.720 --> 28:47.050
Isn't this the poem

669
28:47.620 --> 28:48.790
we just read?

670
28:49.510 --> 28:50.240
Yes.

671
28:50.310 --> 28:52.310
Didn't we just mention Zhuge Liang?

672
28:54.790 --> 28:57.120
You have a great sense of humor, Chairman.

673
28:57.720 --> 28:58.470
Got it.

674
28:58.810 --> 29:06.750
[Fan Shaozeng's Residence, Chongqing]

675
29:21.520 --> 29:22.540
Yuanjing (He Guoguang).

676
29:22.540 --> 29:23.130
Generalissimo.

677
29:23.130 --> 29:25.610
I didn't realize how hard you worked until I came to Chongqing.

678
29:25.240 --> 29:26.400
[He Guoguang Director of the Headquarters Staff Regiment of the Chairman's Field Headquarters, National Military Council of the Kuomintang Government]

679
29:26.060 --> 29:26.990
Generalissimo.

680
29:27.510 --> 29:28.400
What is this?

681
29:29.410 --> 29:30.720
This is the tea I brought for you.

682
29:30.720 --> 29:32.780
Please have a taste, Generalissimo.

683
29:32.920 --> 29:33.590
Tea?

684
29:37.880 --> 29:38.810
Generalissimo.

685
29:38.850 --> 29:41.200
When you sent me to Sichuan, you said

686
29:41.350 --> 29:43.180
you hoped to come to Chongqing next year

687
29:43.180 --> 29:45.640
to taste the new Sweet Dew of Mount Mengding.

688
29:46.140 --> 29:48.070
This is a fresh batch of spring tea.

689
29:48.390 --> 29:50.470
Yuanjing, you are very thoughtful.

690
29:50.760 --> 29:52.620
The tea is indeed freshly picked,

691
29:52.870 --> 29:54.260
but the "bandits"

692
29:55.250 --> 29:57.110
are still the same old "bandits."

693
29:59.670 --> 30:00.800
I remember the tea.

694
30:01.160 --> 30:03.190
But I remember your instructions, even more clearly

695
30:03.190 --> 30:04.410
than I remember this tea.

696
30:04.410 --> 30:05.450
You once said that

697
30:05.750 --> 30:07.910
among the southwestern provinces— Sichuan, Yunnan, and Guizhou—

698
30:07.910 --> 30:09.840
Sichuan is the most important one.

699
30:10.070 --> 30:12.030
We should suppress the Communist Army and stabilize Sichuan.

700
30:12.030 --> 30:13.880
Then we should use Sichuan as our base

701
30:13.880 --> 30:16.000
to extend our control over other southwestern provinces.

702
30:16.000 --> 30:17.960
Since arriving in Sichuan,

703
30:18.790 --> 30:20.920
I haven't forgotten that for a moment.

704
30:21.610 --> 30:22.290
Look at him.

705
30:22.490 --> 30:24.620
If our Party's officials and generals

706
30:24.990 --> 30:26.590
were as devoted as Yuanjing,

707
30:26.810 --> 30:28.570
how could we fail in our cause?

708
30:28.920 --> 30:29.850
Generalissimo.

709
30:29.920 --> 30:31.790
You truly are the wise one!

710
30:31.910 --> 30:32.740
The situation is developing

711
30:32.740 --> 30:34.550
just as you predicted.

712
30:34.830 --> 30:37.270
The Zhu-Mao Communist forces penetrated deep into

713
30:37.270 --> 30:38.390
the Daliangshan and Xiaoliangshan regions between the three rivers.

714
30:38.390 --> 30:39.520
They are now trapped

715
30:40.000 --> 30:42.110
and their complete destruction is imminent.

716
30:42.110 --> 30:42.970
Generalissimo.

717
30:42.970 --> 30:45.450
When the time comes, you can peacefully

718
30:45.790 --> 30:47.560
establish and consolidate your base in the southwest.

719
30:47.560 --> 30:48.390
Good.

720
30:49.750 --> 30:50.640
Yuanjing,

721
30:51.110 --> 30:52.350
keep those two jars

722
30:52.680 --> 30:53.930
of tea for me.

723
30:54.190 --> 30:55.960
After wiping out the Zhu-Mao Communist forces,

724
30:55.960 --> 30:57.360
I'll return to Chongqing again

725
30:57.360 --> 30:59.960
and celebrate your success with tea instead of wine.

726
30:59.960 --> 31:01.160
Yes, Generalissimo.

727
31:06.400 --> 31:08.650
This book, More Essays from a Commonplace Hut,

728
31:08.650 --> 31:09.580
records

729
31:09.610 --> 31:12.650
Shi Dakai's final days by the Dadu River.

730
31:12.860 --> 31:16.230
His fate is much like the fate that awaits Zhu-Mao Communist forces.

731
31:16.230 --> 31:18.680
Could this be merely a coincidence of history?

732
31:18.680 --> 31:19.720
No.

733
31:20.200 --> 31:22.860
This is the inevitable result of being a bandit.

734
31:23.400 --> 31:23.920
I was thinking,

735
31:23.920 --> 31:26.070
if we ever capture Mao Zedong alive,

736
31:26.150 --> 31:28.080
I'll personally hand him this book

737
31:28.460 --> 31:29.620
and make him read it.

738
31:30.420 --> 31:34.070
Do you think he will sigh in despair?

739
31:37.330 --> 31:38.330
Yuanjing,

740
31:38.570 --> 31:39.920
I've finished the book.

741
31:40.920 --> 31:42.710
I hope you'll read it, too.

742
31:47.140 --> 31:48.870
I've made notes in the margins.

743
31:48.880 --> 31:50.410
Thank you, Generalissimo.

744
31:50.620 --> 31:53.020
I'll study it carefully as you instructed,

745
31:53.650 --> 31:55.030
and take your advice to heart.

746
31:55.030 --> 31:55.960
Good.

747
31:56.310 --> 32:02.070
[Mianning County, Liangshan, Sichuan]

748
32:26.480 --> 32:31.370
[Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

749
32:44.470 --> 32:51.610
[Catholic church in Mianning, Liangshan, Sichuan]

750
32:47.640 --> 32:48.790
Come on, put it down here.

751
32:48.790 --> 32:49.920
Put it here, come on.

752
32:52.480 --> 32:53.270
Careful, don't bump it.

753
32:53.270 --> 32:53.750
Slow down.

754
32:53.750 --> 32:54.610
Mind your step.

755
32:55.550 --> 32:55.920
Careful.

756
32:55.920 --> 32:56.240
Okay.

757
32:56.240 --> 32:57.240
Careful.

758
32:59.510 --> 33:00.440
Hello.

759
33:00.440 --> 33:01.110
Hurry up.

760
33:02.240 --> 33:02.960
Hello.

761
33:03.830 --> 33:04.440
Careful.

762
33:04.650 --> 33:06.450
For God's sake,

763
33:07.020 --> 33:08.740
please don't hurt us.

764
33:10.270 --> 33:11.190
She said,

765
33:11.550 --> 33:12.480
for God's sake,

766
33:12.520 --> 33:14.120
please don't hurt them.

767
33:15.850 --> 33:17.130
Please don't worry.

768
33:17.510 --> 33:19.960
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps and Political Commissar of the Central Red Army]

769
33:17.690 --> 33:19.890
We're members of the Communist Party of China,

770
33:19.890 --> 33:21.750
we protect legitimate religious activities

771
33:21.750 --> 33:23.400
and we won't hurt you.

772
33:23.910 --> 33:24.910
Would you allow us

773
33:25.030 --> 33:27.080
to use this place

774
33:27.270 --> 33:28.920
as a temporary command post?

775
33:28.960 --> 33:29.640
Of course.

776
33:29.750 --> 33:30.590
Thank you.

777
33:31.700 --> 33:32.900
He said of course.

778
33:33.330 --> 33:33.850
Good.

779
33:34.070 --> 33:34.660
Here.

780
33:35.810 --> 33:37.140
I'll put it here for you.

781
33:37.480 --> 33:38.080
Slow down.

782
33:38.310 --> 33:39.240
We need another pair of hands here.

783
33:39.240 --> 33:40.500
Give us a hand. Come on.

784
33:43.880 --> 33:45.810
Commander. Political Commissar.

785
33:46.320 --> 33:48.050
We found more than a dozen Yi men

786
33:48.250 --> 33:49.980
in a dungeon in the county town.

787
33:50.910 --> 33:52.370
These are their shackles.

788
34:00.110 --> 34:01.180
Who are they?

789
34:01.410 --> 34:04.010
They're Yi leaders taken hostage in rotation.

790
34:04.410 --> 34:05.940
Taken hostage in rotation?

791
34:06.200 --> 34:07.510
What does that mean?

792
34:07.620 --> 34:09.570
It's a method the local authorities use

793
34:09.570 --> 34:11.300
to control the local Yi people.

794
34:11.400 --> 34:12.750
If a family refuses to comply,

795
34:12.750 --> 34:14.070
they seize one of its leaders

796
34:14.070 --> 34:15.600
and lock him up as a hostage.

797
34:15.739 --> 34:17.810
Family members can take turns being held hostage.

798
34:17.810 --> 34:19.139
A son can be held in his father's place,

799
34:19.139 --> 34:20.400
or a younger brother can take the place of his elder brother.

800
34:20.400 --> 34:22.150
Many of them never make it home.

801
34:22.170 --> 34:23.300
When a hostage dies,

802
34:23.360 --> 34:25.710
someone else is imprisoned to replace them.

803
34:25.710 --> 34:26.440
Xiao Hua,

804
34:27.030 --> 34:28.090
where are they now?

805
34:28.120 --> 34:29.120
Right at the door.

806
34:29.480 --> 34:30.340
Invite them in.

807
34:30.670 --> 34:31.440
Yes.

808
34:37.260 --> 34:38.320
Everyone, come in.

809
34:38.489 --> 34:39.820
Come on in, all of you.

810
35:14.200 --> 35:16.130
These people were locked up

811
35:16.160 --> 35:17.360
in filthy, stinking cells.

812
35:17.360 --> 35:19.160
They were treated like animals.

813
35:19.190 --> 35:20.520
Some weren't even wearing clothes,

814
35:20.520 --> 35:22.930
so they covered themselves with grass.

815
35:23.290 --> 35:24.720
Can we find them some clothes?

816
35:24.720 --> 35:26.030
We seized some clothes earlier

817
35:26.030 --> 35:27.030
at the magistrate's courtyard.

818
35:27.030 --> 35:27.960
Great.

819
35:28.360 --> 35:29.630
Pick out the best ones and bring them here.

820
35:29.630 --> 35:29.980
Yes, sir.

821
35:29.980 --> 35:30.670
Also,

822
35:31.000 --> 35:32.210
prepare some food.

823
35:33.230 --> 35:34.020
Understood.

824
35:39.240 --> 35:39.920
Brothers,

825
35:40.710 --> 35:41.840
come in and sit down.

826
35:41.850 --> 35:42.890
Have a seat.

827
35:43.230 --> 35:44.800
That's right, don't just stand there.

828
35:44.800 --> 35:45.260
Come on.

829
35:45.280 --> 35:46.130
Here, move this a bit.

830
35:46.130 --> 35:46.480
Come on.

831
35:46.480 --> 35:47.250
Take a seat.

832
35:48.780 --> 35:50.180
Come on, be careful.

833
35:51.120 --> 35:51.720
Come here.

834
35:52.100 --> 35:52.710
Here.

835
35:53.190 --> 35:54.100
Slow down.

836
35:54.230 --> 35:54.750
Okay.

837
35:55.680 --> 35:56.280
Come here.

838
35:57.690 --> 35:58.370
Come in.

839
36:47.600 --> 36:48.800
You must be starving.

840
36:48.920 --> 36:49.950
Go ahead and eat.

841
36:51.350 --> 36:52.300
Don't eat.

842
36:54.030 --> 36:56.560
Leader, they're afraid the food is poisoned.

843
37:00.370 --> 37:01.040
Look.

844
37:10.480 --> 37:11.610
Go ahead. It's safe.

845
37:12.620 --> 37:12.960
Eat.

846
37:12.960 --> 37:13.760
Don't eat!

847
37:13.950 --> 37:15.610
Don't you know it's poisoned?

848
37:16.920 --> 37:18.980
They're still afraid it's poisoned.

849
37:22.300 --> 37:24.180
Young man, how about this?

850
37:24.880 --> 37:26.010
You point to a piece,

851
37:26.150 --> 37:27.400
and I'll eat it myself. How about that?

852
37:27.400 --> 37:28.260
What did he say?

853
37:28.400 --> 37:29.480
You point to a piece,

854
37:29.480 --> 37:31.540
and he'll eat it to show you it's safe.

855
37:31.590 --> 37:32.280
Qie.

856
37:32.810 --> 37:33.300
Come on.

857
37:40.520 --> 37:41.210
This piece?

858
37:41.940 --> 37:43.790
Okay, this piece.

859
37:47.550 --> 37:48.110
Eat.

860
37:48.880 --> 37:49.630
Xiao Hua.

861
37:57.650 --> 37:59.080
Come here.

862
38:00.100 --> 38:00.680
Slow down.

863
38:00.680 --> 38:01.610
There's plenty.

864
38:02.920 --> 38:03.710
Eat slowly.

865
38:11.940 --> 38:12.500
Come on.

866
38:12.520 --> 38:13.920
Quick, drink some water.

867
38:15.400 --> 38:15.840
Here.

868
38:16.510 --> 38:17.190
Here, pass it around.

869
38:17.190 --> 38:18.850
Don't you know it's poisoned?

870
38:19.150 --> 38:19.630
Don't move!

871
38:19.630 --> 38:20.360
Sit down!

872
38:20.760 --> 38:21.550
Step back!

873
38:21.880 --> 38:23.550
Put it down! Step back!

874
38:23.980 --> 38:24.750
Put it down!

875
38:25.150 --> 38:27.610
Leader, they're just afraid it's poisoned.

876
38:27.890 --> 38:30.330
Bring the water here.

877
38:31.400 --> 38:32.120
Here.

878
38:35.790 --> 38:36.420
Okay.

879
38:52.540 --> 38:53.250
This is safe to drink, see?

880
38:53.250 --> 38:53.960
Go ahead.

881
38:54.220 --> 38:55.700
Come, take it.

882
38:56.470 --> 38:56.950
Here.

883
39:08.230 --> 39:09.150
Clothes are here.

884
39:09.150 --> 39:09.720
All right.

885
39:09.720 --> 39:11.590
Later, you should put these on.

886
39:12.070 --> 39:12.800
I hope you don't mind these clothes.

887
39:12.800 --> 39:14.280
They are for you to wear.

888
39:14.980 --> 39:15.830
Hand them out.

889
39:16.360 --> 39:17.360
Put them on. Here.

890
39:18.170 --> 39:19.100
Pass them along.

891
39:20.070 --> 39:20.470
Right.

892
39:20.590 --> 39:21.000
Put them on.

893
39:21.000 --> 39:21.530
Go ahead.

894
39:28.050 --> 39:29.010
What do you want?

895
39:29.040 --> 39:32.240
Leader, he wants to know what you're going to do with them.

896
39:33.600 --> 39:34.600
Get dressed

897
39:34.750 --> 39:35.670
and you can go home.

898
39:35.670 --> 39:36.280
What did he say?

899
39:36.280 --> 39:38.680
He said you can go home once you're dressed.

900
39:38.890 --> 39:39.690
That's funny.

901
39:39.700 --> 39:41.330
Do you really think we can go home?

902
39:41.330 --> 39:44.210
Leader, he thinks we might be planning an ambush.

903
39:47.580 --> 39:48.580
Young man,

904
39:49.290 --> 39:52.400
do you see the red star on my cap?

905
39:52.690 --> 39:54.210
This red star here

906
39:54.800 --> 39:55.820
represents the Red Army.

907
39:55.820 --> 39:58.490
Most of us in the Red Army are Han Chinese,

908
39:58.830 --> 39:59.940
but just like you,

909
40:00.080 --> 40:01.540
we come from poor families

910
40:01.760 --> 40:04.920
and have suffered under Han warlords, too.

911
40:05.030 --> 40:05.720
What did he say?

912
40:05.720 --> 40:08.320
Do you see the red star on his cap?

913
40:08.340 --> 40:10.400
Anyone wearing that red star cap is a Red Army soldier.

914
40:10.400 --> 40:11.630
Although they are Han Chinese,

915
40:11.630 --> 40:14.320
they come from poor families, too.

916
40:14.550 --> 40:15.810
They're not here to beat us

917
40:15.810 --> 40:16.960
or kill us.

918
40:17.040 --> 40:19.210
They are here to help us.

919
40:21.270 --> 40:22.830
The Red Army has come here

920
40:23.030 --> 40:24.190
to help you

921
40:24.630 --> 40:26.360
break free from those shackles.

922
40:26.360 --> 40:29.360
They're not here to attack or kill us.

923
40:29.360 --> 40:30.920
They're here to help us.

924
40:31.190 --> 40:32.190
Did you hear that?

925
40:32.660 --> 40:35.020
Young man, my name is Liu Bocheng.

926
40:35.260 --> 40:36.570
You and your people

927
40:36.780 --> 40:38.410
can go home without fear.

928
40:38.710 --> 40:39.880
If anyone wearing

929
40:40.070 --> 40:42.440
this kind of cap stops you on the way,

930
40:42.590 --> 40:43.650
just tell them that

931
40:43.710 --> 40:45.900
Liu Bocheng has given you permission to go home.

932
40:45.900 --> 40:46.760
What did he say?

933
40:46.760 --> 40:48.360
His name is Liu Bocheng.

934
40:48.510 --> 40:51.550
If anyone wearing a red star cap

935
40:51.550 --> 40:54.710
stops you on the way, you just tell them

936
40:54.880 --> 40:58.510
that Liu Bocheng said you're free to go home.

937
41:00.110 --> 41:01.000
Go home.

